From: ane-stack
Subject: [PATCH 0004] milc: stop routing every .mlpackage to the shard loader

cmd_run decided "is this a shard bundle?" with `path.join("manifest.json").exists()`.
Every CoreML .mlpackage contains `Manifest.json` (capital M). macOS APFS is
case-insensitive by default, so the test matched ordinary packages too, and

  milc run model.mlpackage --units ane

failed with `infer manifest: kind is not "milshards"`. The package path now
also requires the absence of `Data/com.apple.CoreML/model.mlmodel`, which no
shard bundle has.

Verified after the fix: a stateful IR-compiled package compiles through
coreml.framework and runs on cpu+ane (3 steps, median 99.42us).

Upstream: 20f097fb34969cd577342a4d7996fbf5464998c8
--- a/crates/milc/src/main.rs
+++ b/crates/milc/src/main.rs
@@ -1514,7 +1514,15 @@
         eprintln!("milc run: needs <pkg.mlpackage>");
         return ExitCode::from(2);
     };
-    if path.join("manifest.json").exists() {
+    // FORK(ane-stack): a shard bundle carries a lowercase `manifest.json`,
+    // while every CoreML `.mlpackage` carries `Manifest.json`. macOS APFS is
+    // case-insensitive by default, so the bare existence test matched the
+    // package too and sent every plain package down the shard loader
+    // ("infer manifest: kind is not \"milshards\""). Match the exact name.
+    // Upstream: 20f097f.
+    if path.join("manifest.json").exists()
+        && !path.join("Data/com.apple.CoreML/model.mlmodel").exists()
+    {
         return run_sharded(&path, units, steps);
     }
     let spec_path = path.join("Data/com.apple.CoreML/model.mlmodel");
